If I was a part of SPOTIFY development team then a feature I'd Introduce: AI-Powered Contextual Listening

What it is:
A feature that adapts music recommendations based not only on listening history but also on the user's current context, such as studying, commuting, working out, relaxing, or traveling.

Why I'd introduce it:

Creates a more personalized and relevant user experience.
Reduces the time users spend searching for the right music.
Increases user engagement and listening duration.
Differentiates Spotify from competitors through smarter recommendations.
Strengthens user loyalty by making the platform feel more intuitive.
Feature I'd Improve/Remove: Overly Repetitive Recommendations

Current issue:
Spotify often recommends the same popular songs, artists, or playlists repeatedly, which can limit music discovery.

Why I'd change it:

Users may become bored with repetitive suggestions.
New and emerging artists get less visibility.
Discovery is a key reason people use music streaming platforms.
A more diverse recommendation engine would improve user satisfaction.

Proposed solution:

Introduce a "Fresh Discovery" mode.
Allow users to control how much familiar vs. new content appears in recommendations.
Reduce the frequency of songs that users repeatedly skip.
